  "claim": "The breed of dog that a Bavarian Hound is crossed with to produce a Bavarian Mountain Hound is descended from bloodhounds unlike another breed of dog. Oscar the Grouch is an example of this other breed of dog.",
  "evidencia": "Page: Greater Swiss Mountain Dog. Sentence: The Greater Swiss Mountain Dog (German: \"Grosser Schweizer Sennenhund\" or French: \"Grand Bouvier Suisse\" ) is a dog breed which was developed in the Swiss Alps.\nPage: Greater Swiss Mountain Dog. Sentence: Greater Swiss Mountain Dogs are almost certainly the result of indigenous dogs mating with large mastiff types brought to Switzerland by foreign settlers.\nPage: Hanover Hound. Sentence: The Hanover Hound is a breed of dog sometimes referred to as a Hanoverian Hound.\nPage: Hanover Hound. Sentence: It is a hunting and tracking dog descended from bloodhounds of medieval times.\nPage: Oscar the Grouch (dog). Sentence: Also seen on the opening promo for the Dog Show on the USA Network and on Bloomberg, Oscar is a top-ranked Greater Swiss Mountain Dog.\nPage: Bavarian Mountain Hound. Sentence: It is a cross between the Bavarian Hound and the Hanover Hound.",
