        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "9d0b01c8-7152-5d3a-a127-ee559a622e28",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Dog breeds: Greater Swiss Mountain Dog, Hanover Hound, Bavarian Mountain Hound\n- Dogs: Oscar the Grouch\n- Places: Swiss Alps, Switzerland\n- Concepts: breed origins, hunting and tracking\n\nFacts:\n- The Greater Swiss Mountain Dog is a dog breed developed in the Swiss Alps.\n- Greater Swiss Mountain Dogs are almost certainly the result of indigenous dogs mating with large mastiff-type dogs brought to Switzerland by foreign settlers.\n- The Hanover Hound is a dog breed also called the Hanoverian Hound.\n- The Hanover Hound is a hunting and tracking dog descended from medieval bloodhounds.\n- The Bavarian Mountain Hound is a cross between the Bavarian Hound and the Hanover Hound.\n- Oscar the Grouch is a top-ranked Greater Swiss Mountain Dog that was seen on opening promos for the Dog Show on USA Network and on Bloomberg.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "9beb34ff-39e0-5bdb-a1bf-c0f79760777a",
        "text": "Page: Greater Swiss Mountain Dog. Sentence: The Greater Swiss Mountain Dog (German: \"Grosser Schweizer Sennenhund\" or French: \"Grand Bouvier Suisse\" ) is a dog breed which was developed in the Swiss Alps.\nPage: Greater Swiss Mountain Dog. Sentence: Greater Swiss Mountain Dogs are almost certainly the result of indigenous dogs mating with large mastiff types brought to Switzerland by foreign settlers.\nPage: Hanover Hound. Sentence: The Hanover Hound is a breed of dog sometimes referred to as a Hanoverian Hound.\nPage: Hanover Hound. Sentence: It is a hunting and tracking dog descended from bloodhounds of medieval times.\nPage: Oscar the Grouch (dog). Sentence: Also seen on the opening promo for the Dog Show on the USA Network and on Bloomberg, Oscar is a top-ranked Greater Swiss Mountain Dog.\nPage: Bavarian Mountain Hound. Sentence: It is a cross between the Bavarian Hound and the Hanover Hound.",
